-- title:
--   Odd multiples cover a finite odd cyclic group up to sign
-- statement:
--   Let $Q$ be a finite abelian group of odd cardinality generated by $\alpha$, and let $\delta\in Q$. Then
--
--   $$\exists n\in\mathbb N,\quad n\text{ odd},\qquad n\alpha=\delta\text{ or }n\alpha=-\delta.$$
--
--   This finds an odd-degree return to either sign of any target.
-- source:
--   Alexandre Couret, https://github.com/alexcour/couret-finite-verifications/blob/65b828d9ffd016ce2a1b05403f303fa5f948c10f/research/correspondants_20261013/lean/CayleyTwoColourNecessity.lean#L42-L70, lines 42–70; source file SHA-256 7675ca2a1f08e8c6a20617d181810b5c2b6a4f0cffcf96b93678cb0bc9c7869d; theorem Couret.CayleyNecessity.odd_multiple_or_neg_of_cyclic

